let __v_355 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"back\",{\"$tuple\":[\"back\",\"lower back\",\"spine\",\"backache\"]},\"Most back pain is muscular and settles in two to six weeks, and staying active is what helps most: keep walking and carry on with your usual jobs as far as you can rather than taking to your bed, and take paracetamol or ibuprofen if you can. See a GP if it is no better in a fortnight, or today if you cannot pass urine, have numbness between your legs, or it came on after a fall.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"knee\",{\"$tuple\":[\"knee\",\"kneecap\"]},\"A sore knee is usually a strain or the kneecap tracking badly: ease off running, stairs and kneeling, ice it for 20 minutes at a time with a cloth round it for the first two days, then keep it moving gently. Get it looked at if it gives way, locks, or you cannot put your weight on it.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"shoulder\",{\"$tuple\":[\"shoulder\",\"shoulders\",\"shoulder blade\",\"rotator cuff\"]},\"Most shoulder pain is a strained or trapped tendon, worse when you reach overhead or lie on that side: keep using the arm as far as is comfortable, warm it before you use it, and do the pendulum swing (lean forward, let the arm hang, circle it slowly) a few times a day. See a GP if you cannot lift the arm at all or it started after a fall.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"neck\",{\"$tuple\":[\"neck\",\"stiff neck\"]},\"A stiff neck is usually muscular, from posture or sleeping awkwardly: heat, gentle stretches and a look at your screen height help, and a soft collar for a day or two is fine but not longer, because the muscles need to work. Get seen the same day if it comes with a fever, a bad headache, or light hurting your eyes.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"hip\",{\"$tuple\":[\"hip\",\"hips\"]},\"Hip pain in an adult is usually the joint or the tendon over the outside of the hip bone: keep walking as far as is comfortable, sit with your knees lower than your hips, and take a painkiller before a walk rather than after. See a GP if it hurts when you are resting or at night, or you have started to limp.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"ankle\",{\"$tuple\":[\"ankle\",\"ankles\"]},\"An ankle sprain wants ice for 20 minutes at a time for the first two days, a support wrap and the foot up when you sit, then gentle movement and a slow return to walking on it. Most settle in two to six weeks, and the swelling can take months. Get it looked at the same day if you cannot put any weight on it, it swells badly, or it looks crooked.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"foot\",{\"$tuple\":[\"foot\",\"feet\",\"heel\",\"heels\",\"arch\",\"plantar\"]},\"Foot pain is often the plantar fascia, the band under the arch, worst on your first steps in the morning: stretch the calf against a wall before you stand up, roll the arch on a cold bottle, and wear shoes with a firm sole indoors too. A heel that hurts all day, or a foot that is red and hot, needs looking at.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"wrist\",{\"$tuple\":[\"wrist\",\"wrists\",\"hand\",\"hands\",\"thumb\",\"fingers\"]},\"Wrist and hand pain is usually an overused tendon or a nerve pressed by the way you grip and type: take breaks, keep the wrist straight rather than bent, and try a support splint from the pharmacy at night. Pins and needles in the fingers that wake you is worth a GP visit.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"elbow\",{\"$tuple\":[\"elbow\",\"elbows\",\"tennis elbow\"]},\"Elbow pain on the outside is tennis elbow, an overused tendon, and it settles over weeks to months once you rest from the gripping and lifting that sets it off: a strap just below the elbow and slow strengthening with a light weight help. See a GP if it is no better in six weeks.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"arm\",{\"$tuple\":[\"arm\",\"arms\",\"upper arm\",\"forearm\"]},\"Most arm pain is a muscle strain or the ache a day after lifting, and some of it comes down from a sore shoulder or elbow: keep using it as far as is comfortable and take a painkiller if you can. See a GP if the arm is weak or numb, and treat a heavy left arm with tightness in the chest, sweating or breathlessness as an emergency.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"ribs\",{\"$tuple\":[\"rib\",\"ribs\",\"ribcage\",\"rib cage\",\"ribs hurt\"]},\"A rib that hurts when you breathe in, cough or press it is usually bruised, not broken, and it mends the same way either way: keep breathing normally rather than in shallow sips, take paracetamol or ibuprofen, and press a cushion against that side when you cough. It eases over three to six weeks. Get seen the same day if you are breathless or coughing blood.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"tailbone\",{\"$tuple\":[\"tailbone\",\"tail bone\",\"coccyx\",\"sacrum\"]},\"A sore tailbone is usually a knock from a fall or hours sitting on a hard chair, and it mends slowly - a few weeks, sometimes a couple of months. Sit on a soft or doughnut cushion, tilt forward a little rather than leaning back onto it, and take paracetamol or ibuprofen; a warm bath helps the muscles around it. See a GP if it is no better after a few weeks, or if there is numbness or bleeding.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"toe\",{\"$tuple\":[\"toe\",\"toes\",\"big toe\"]},\"Most toe pain is a stub, a bruise under the nail or an ingrown edge: soak it in warm salty water, wear shoes with room in them and take paracetamol. A big toe that goes red, hot and swollen overnight, often at night, is gout - that one wants seeing this week, and sooner if you have diabetes and it looks infected.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"collarbone\",{\"$tuple\":[\"collarbone\",\"collar bone\",\"clavicle\"]},\"A collarbone that hurts after a knock usually mends in a sling over four to six weeks, and the pain often eases before the bone has joined: keep the hand and elbow moving gently, sleep propped up a little and take paracetamol. Have it looked at with an X-ray if you cannot lift the arm, the bone looks out of line, or it hurts too much to sleep.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"groin\",{\"$tuple\":[\"groin\",\"adductor\"]},\"A sore groin is usually a pulled muscle from twisting, kicking or turning quickly: give the sport that set it off a fortnight off, ice it for 20 minutes at a time for the first two days, then stretch and strengthen gently. Get a lump or a bulge that appears when you cough or lift looked at - that is a hernia - and get a sudden severe pain in one side seen the same day.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"leg\",{\"$tuple\":[\"leg\",\"legs\",\"calf\",\"calves\",\"thigh\",\"thighs\",\"hamstring\",\"shin\"]},\"A pulled thigh or calf muscle, or the ache that lands a day after squats, wants the same start: rest it, ice it for 20 minutes at a time for two days, then gentle stretching and a slow return to what you were doing, with the leg kept up when you sit. Calf pain with a hot, swollen leg, or a shin that hurts to touch after a knock, needs looking at.\"]}]}")?;
