let __v_2780 = Value::from("it aches after years of use, is stiff first thing and eases as you move, and the treatment is using the joint rather than sparing it. Walking, swimming or cycling and a little strength work a few times a week keep the muscles that support the joint strong, and paracetamol with an ibuprofen gel handles a flare better than most tablets sold for arthritis. Glucosamine and cod liver oil have not held up in trials, no diet cures it, and cold, damp weather can make it ache more without damaging the joint; losing weight if you are carrying extra takes real load off knees and hips. Stiffness that lasts more than an hour in the morning, or a joint that is hot, red and swollen, is the inflammatory kind and wants a GP soon - ask about physiotherapy, and about a steroid injection for one joint that keeps flaring.");
